# ── session state: these three MOVED OUT of the repository on 2026-07-30 ──────
#
# They now live under ~/.nexa/workspaces/<id>/ (or $NEXA_STATE_DIR) — see stateRoot in
# scripts/hooks/roots.mjs, and board/3-build/002 for why. Being merely gitignored was not
# enough: git will not restore what it does not track, so `git clean -xfd` destroyed the only
# copy of every prompt ever typed, and the prompt log — which has carried a VPS root password
# and an OAuth code — sat inside a directory a `git add -f` or a zip could sweep up.
#
# **The entries stay** for two reasons: a clone made before the move still has the old
# directories until a hook migrates them, and an entry removed here would silently make the
# next stale copy committable. They cost nothing when the paths do not exist.
#
# To keep a day deliberately, copy it in on purpose:
#   cp ~/.nexa/workspaces/<id>/prompts/YYYY-MM-DD.md docs/prompts/ && git add -f docs/prompts/YYYY-MM-DD.md
docs/prompts/
docs/compactions/
docs/.prompt-check-state.json


# Council runs are YOUR deliberations, not this package's. One worked example lives in
# docs/examples/council-run.md; everything else stays local.
.council/runs/

# The one-shot discard override — never committed, consumed on use.
.nexa-allow-discard

# The council is VENDORED at plugin/scripts/council/ (MIT, pinned in .vendored-from) and is
# tracked deliberately — it is a core feature, and a core feature that needs a second install
# step is not one. Refresh it with nexa-council-update.

# kill-audit's crash journal: the original bytes of the control it is currently mutating.
# Present only while a run is in flight, or after one was killed — the next run restores from it
# and deletes it. Never committed; it is machine state, not a record.
.nexa-kill-audit-inflight.json
